# SPA fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# expo export --platform web with expo-router's default "single" output mode
# produces one index.html and a JS bundle. All client-side routing (e.g.
# /listing/:id) is handled by JavaScript. If a user opens a direct link or
# hard-refreshes any sub-path, the static host must serve index.html rather
# than returning a 404 — otherwise every shared listing link is broken.
#
# Asset paths are served before these rules ever run (the host always serves
# a real file if it exists), but the explicit negative patterns below make
# the intent clear and guard against any host-specific ordering edge cases.
#
# Rules are evaluated top-to-bottom; the first match wins.

# Pass real static asset directories straight through (200 = serve as-is).
/_expo/*   /_expo/:splat  200
/assets/*  /assets/:splat 200

# Everything else — including /listing/abc, /conversation/xyz, hard-refreshed
# tab paths, etc. — gets index.html with a 200 (not a 301 redirect, so the
# browser URL stays correct and the JS router takes over).
/*         /index.html    200
